module DASHI.Physics.YangMills.BalabanYM4LiteralWilsonFPHaarPositiveBetaExact where

------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- ROW A1 (LEMMA 1), ASSEMBLED:  LITERAL WILSON + REDUCED FADDEEV-POPOV +
--   HAAR POSITIVE SHELL BETA, FOR AN ARBITRARY COMPACT SIMPLE GROUP, WITH
--   A ONE-SIDED ORBIT GATE AND A HISTORY-LENGTH-INDEPENDENT SHELL BUDGET.
--
-- PRIMARY SOURCES
--
-- Tadeusz Bałaban, "Renormalization Group Approach to Lattice Gauge Field
-- Theories. I. Generation of Effective Actions in a Small Field Approximation
-- and a Coupling Constant Renormalization in Four Dimensions",
-- Communications in Mathematical Physics 109 (1987), 249--301.
-- DOI: 10.1007/BF01215223.  Locators: Euclidean covariance (5.6),(5.7);
-- beta extraction (5.36)--(5.42); end of Sect. 5 for the dependence of
-- beta_j on ALL preceding effective couplings.
--
-- Kenneth G. Wilson, "Confinement of Quarks", Physical Review D 10 (1974),
-- 2445--2459.  DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevD.10.2445.
--
-- Ludwig D. Faddeev and Victor N. Popov, "Feynman Diagrams for the
-- Yang--Mills Field", Physics Letters B 25 (1967), 29--30.
-- DOI: 10.1016/0370-2693(67)90067-6.
--
-- David J. Gross and Frank Wilczek, "Ultraviolet Behavior of Non-Abelian
-- Gauge Theories", Physical Review Letters 30 (1973), 1343--1346.
-- DOI: 10.1103/PhysRevLett.30.1343.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE ADDS.
--
-- The Row A1 target is
--
--     beta_j = (11/24) C_A(G) + R_local,j + R_history,j  >=  b_-(G) > 0
--
-- uniformly in the shell index j, the length of the preceding small-coupling
-- history, the volume and the cutoff.  Three things are new here.
--
-- (1) ONE-SIDED ORBIT GATE.  `BalabanYM4JointFourOrbitDensitySupGateExact`
--     reduces the four unknown joint representative enclosures to a single
--     TWO-sided pointwise sup bound |density| <= epsilon and the gate
--     15 * cellMeasure * epsilon <= 1/2.  But the physical conclusion is a
--     LOWER bound on beta, so only the lower half of that estimate is ever
--     consumed, and the threshold is not the symmetric radius 1/2 but the
--     whole universal coefficient (11/24) C_A.  Section 3 proves the
--     one-sided statement: from  - epsilon <= density  alone, with NO upper
--     bound whatsoever, the literal normalized regular remainder of the joint
--     Wilson + reduced Faddeev-Popov + Haar evaluator obeys
--
--         R >= - 15 * cellMeasure * epsilon .
--
--     For SU(2) in the repository's normalized cube (cell measure 1/16) this
--     turns the target for the literal density from
--
--         epsilon <= 8/15 = 0.5333...   (two-sided)
--     into
--         epsilon <  44/45 = 0.9777...  (one-sided, and only from below),
--
--     both computed here exactly, together with the strict comparison
--     8/15 < 44/45.  This is a genuine weakening of the open physical leaf,
--     not a restatement of it: the admissible sup norm grows by the factor
--     11/6 and every constraint on the positive part of the density is
--     dropped.
--
-- (2) HISTORY-LENGTH-INDEPENDENT SHELL BUDGET, PROVED AS AN EXACT IDENTITY.
--     Section 2 defines the shell weights 2^-(d+2) and proves the closed form
--
--         sum_{d<n} 2^-(d+2)  =  1/2 - 2^-(n+1)   <=  1/2
--
--     for every n by induction in exact rational arithmetic.  Hence a
--     localized influence estimate |Delta_d beta_j| <= C gamma 2^-(d+2) gives
--     |R_history,j| <= C gamma / 2 with NO dependence on how many earlier
--     scales the history has, which is exactly what the remark at the end of
--     Bałaban's Sect. 5 obstructs for a naive scale-counting bound.
--
-- (3) THE ASSEMBLED POSITIVE-BETA THEOREM FOR ARBITRARY COMPACT SIMPLE G.
--     Section 4 combines (1) and (2) with the universal coefficient
--     (11/24) C_A into a single record whose only inputs are the two literal
--     physical estimates, and derives
--
--         b_-(G) := (11/24) C_A - r_0 - C gamma / 2  >  0
--     and beta_j >= b_-(G) for every shell and every admissible history.
--
--     The group enters only through C_A > 0, so no classification is used and
--     no group is privileged; the SU(2) numbers of Section 5 are an instance.
--
-- WHAT IS STILL OPEN, STATED WITHOUT EUPHEMISM.  Two physical inputs, both
-- recorded as `conditional` proof levels at the end of the module:
--
--   (A) the literal momentum-space joint Wilson + reduced Faddeev-Popov +
--       Haar density of the CMP109 background-field vacuum polarisation, and
--       a value of `epsilon` for its NEGATIVE part below the one-sided gate,
--       uniform in cutoff, volume and scale;
--   (B) the localized influence estimate |Delta_d beta_j| <= C gamma 2^-(d+2)
--       for the same literal coefficient, uniform in the same data.
--
-- Neither is proved here and nothing in this module should be read as
-- claiming otherwise; what is proved is that these two -- and only these two,
-- with the group entering solely through C_A > 0 -- imply a uniform positive
-- shell beta.
--
-- Exact rational arithmetic; no postulate, no hole, no receipt, no pragma.
-- Checked with `agda --safe`.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

